<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="49848" href="schedule/2018/spring/PSYC/593/49848.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2018" href="schedule/2018.xml">2018</calendarYear><term id="120181" href="schedule/2018/spring.xml">Spring 2018</term><subject id="PSYC" href="schedule/2018/spring/PSYC.xml">Psychology</subject><course id="593" href="schedule/2018/spring/PSYC/593.xml">Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>SL2</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Moral Psychology</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Intensive analysis of issues in the psychological study of morality. Among others topics, the course will cover development of moral judgment, classic and modern outlooks, major theories and recent advances, moral emotions, moral hypocrisy, morality and political ideology, morality and the law, morality and the environment, morality and religion, moral dilemmas, morality in consumer contexts, and the study of praise and blame.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2018-01-16Z</startDate><endDate>2018-05-02Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>10:00 AM</start><end>11:50 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>T      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>508</roomNumber><buildingName>Psychology Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Laurent" firstName="S">Laurent, S</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>